  {
    "ref": "324f9c483d9b4a11249c47888b40fb5cc691be7f",
    "commit": "commit 324f9c483d9b4a11249c47888b40fb5cc691be7f\nAuthor:     Max Engel <max@awecelot.com>\nAuthorDate: Thu Sep 10 23:41:39 2026 +0000\nCommit:     Max Engel <max@awecelot.com>\nCommitDate: Thu Sep 10 23:41:39 2026 +0000\n\n    Add a unit-test binary for the pure cloud text\n    \n    #120 box 4: the cheapest test this project can run. 19 cases, 162\n    assertions, four thousandths of a second, and no image, no VM and no\n    device between writing a parser and knowing what it does with junk.\n    \n    What is covered is what nobody types twice: every \">>> \" shape the\n    scripts print, including a line missing its field, a why with a\n    trailing full stop, the transfer page's markers this reader must not\n    claim, and a line that only looks like one; each stamp shape both\n    writers emit, plus an empty file, a one-field file, an epoch of zero\n    and bytes that are not a stamp at all; the ten-second window that makes\n    two stamps the same run, at 10 and at 11 either side; D-UI-035's worked\n    example shortening to three candidate lines; a hostname with spaces,\n    with UTF-8, with hyphens at both ends, at 70 characters and at the\n    truncation that would leave a trailing hyphen.\n    \n    Proved to fail before it was trusted: widening the origin window to 11,\n    the hostname limit to 64, and shortenWhy's dash to \" -- \" fails 3 cases\n    and 7 assertions; reverting them passes again.\n    \n    doctest 2.4.12 as a single header in external/doctest, the latest of\n    the 2.4 line. The target is es-unit-tests, behind ES_BUILD_TESTS\n    (default OFF, so an image build never builds or links it), and\n    es-app/tests/unit/CMakeLists.txt stands on its own as well -- which is\n    how it is meant to be run, since the top-level CMakeLists cannot\n    configure on a host without SDL, OpenGL, freetype and curl. The binary\n    compiles the tests, CloudText.cpp and StringUtil.cpp, and nothing else\n    of EmulationStation.\n    \n    The i18n target's xgettext runs over all of es-app, so the tests are in\n    its path: they are pure ASCII and carry no _(), and the sweep over the\n    tree is clean.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UGcYBCTGThqS2LHELXjYQX\n"
  },
